{
  "title": "Hemoglobin\u2013resting-pulse coupling did not establish incremental tiredness prediction across separate NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "Adding a source-standardized hemoglobin-by-resting-pulse product changed external-sample Brier loss from 0.122469527 to 0.122630777; baseline-minus-augmented gain -0.000161250 (two-sample stratified-PSU bootstrap95% interval -0.001090280 to 0.000105294). Incremental predictive benefit for frequent tiredness was not demonstrated. Source4819 and target4962 adults from separately recruited NHANES2007\u20132008/2009\u20132010. Small source CV gain did not transfer. Corrected SAS-zero parsing,author self-checks and clean rerun;AI-authored,not independently peer reviewed.",
